    cover_note='Welcome back. In Session 3 we learned to judge a prediction: false alarms, misses, and the score on cases the system never saw. Today we turn to the largest pile of information most organisations hold, which is text: messages from customers, contracts, reports and recorded calls, in English and in our own languages. The question is: what can AI do with them? We start in a Ugandan legal library, build the four language jobs from drawings, tour six industries, and watch a search find the right clause from a plain description. Then you add a pile of your own text to your portfolio.',
